  <body>
    <h1>Chocolate spread</h1>
    <p>Classic Homemade <a href="https://media.istockphoto.com/id/92064416/photo/poop-on-a-shingle.jpg?s=1024x1024&w=is&k=20&c=GHF5JD9luu9Kb131eNrabYli8EGv1Jjfp8RorPxpgVY=">Hazelnut Chocolate Spread</a> (Nutella-Style)</p>
    <h2>Ingredients</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>250g (8 oz) raw, skinless hazelnuts (or roasted hazelnuts)</li>
      <li> 1/4 cup (30g) Dutch-processed unsweetened cocoa powder</li>
      <li>3/4 cup (90g) icing sugar (powdered sugar)</li>
      <li>2 tbsp hazelnut oil or neutral vegetable oil</li>
      <li>1 tsp vanilla extract</li>
      <li>A pinch of salt</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Instructions</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Preheat your oven to 180°C (350°F). Spread the hazelnuts on a baking tray and roast for 8 minutes until golden and fragrant.</li>
      <li>Transfer the warm hazelnuts to a food processor or blender. Process on low speed until they break into crumbs, then increase the speed until the oils release and form a smooth, liquid nut butter.</li>
      <li>Add the cocoa powder, icing sugar, oil, vanilla extract, and salt.</li>
      <li>Blend on high until the mixture is completely smooth and glossy.</li>
      <li> Transfer to a clean glass jar and store at room temperature (refrigerating can make it stiff or grainy).</li>
    </ol>
  </body>
</html>
